# Where this board's logs go.
#
# By default they go nowhere but RAM. /var/log is a tmpfs, so every line the
# kernel and bmcd write is lost at the next boot -- which is precisely when
# you want to read them. The 2026-09-09 mdns outage was diagnosed from
# /var/log/messages on a board that had not yet been rebooted; had it been
# power-cycled first, the 825 "conflicting name detected" lines that gave the
# mechanism away would not have existed.
#
# Writing them to the overlay instead is NOT the fix. The overlay is UBI on a
# 2040-eraseblock NAND with five free, and a log file is the one workload
# guaranteed to keep growing.
#
# The fix is to send them somewhere else. Uncomment and point this at a
# collector that speaks syslog over UDP -- VictoriaLogs with
# `-syslog.listenAddr.udp`, or anything else:
#
#   SYSLOGD_ARGS="-R logs.example:514"
#
# Add -L to keep logging locally as well, which is worth it: the local copy is
# what you read over SSH when the network is the thing that broke.
#
#   SYSLOGD_ARGS="-R logs.example:514 -L"
#
# Left unset on purpose. A default pointing at a host that does not exist would
# make every boot wait on a DNS lookup for a collector nobody configured.
